# Copy this file to configure Resizo's environment.
#   Local dev (Next.js auto-loads this file):  cp .env.example .env.local
#   Docker Compose (env_file: .env):            cp .env.example .env
#
# There is nothing required in here, and that is the point.
#
# Resizo processes every image in the visitor's browser: no upload, no accounts,
# no database, no cache, no rate limiter, no object store. The server serves
# static pages and the WASM codecs and does no image work at all, so it holds no
# credentials for anything.
#
# The Upstash and Vercel Blob variables that used to live here went with the
# image routes. If you find UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL, UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN or
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN still set in a deployment, they are unread and can be
# removed from it.

# Optional. Set by Vercel automatically; only used to label the running build in
# GET /api/health. Anything unset falls back to 'dev'.
# VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA=
